From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 10:42:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06888/11362] [outer-loop] implement run-local cross-game
 mechanic ledger (SS2.1-2.3, off by default)

Builds the RunLocalMechanicLedger scoped in docs/research-notes/
arc-agi3-run-local-cross-game-adaptation-scope-2026-07-12.md, per the
operator ruling recorded there clearing the memorization question:
learning a mechanic class's behavior from this run's own concurrent
play is fine; replaying a memorized per-game action sequence is not.
This ledger does neither of the forbidden things -- it never touches
ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml and never persists past the process.

RunLocalMechanicLedger: thread-safe (lock-protected), in-process,
module-level singleton. Required because Swarm.main() runs every game's
agent concurrently on its own thread within one process -- confirmed
against the REAL scored submission path (scripts/kaggle/submission_
kernel/main.py), not just the offline reference framework. Verified with
a real 50-thread/20-writes-each concurrency stress test: zero lost
updates.

Wired into _maybe_route_from_transitions: when CARNOT_ARC_RUN_LOCAL_
ADAPTATION=1 (off by default), each game contributes its own
(mechanic_class, approach, outcome_proxy) to the ledger, and consults
OTHER concurrently-running games' accumulated evidence for a small,
bounded confidence bonus (max 0.2) on top of the existing per-game gate
-- only after >=3 distinct games of that mechanic class have
contributed (_RUN_LOCAL_MIN_SAMPLES), an explicitly weak signal, not a
statistically significant one.

The outcome proxy is honestly labeled as a cheap scaffold (did any of
the first 8 transitions advance the level), not the real RHAE scoring
formula -- the scope doc's SS2.4 validation harness should measure
against the real formula for its own headline claim.

Still off by default. Per the scope's own Phase Prototype + Empirical
Validation + Adversarial Check discipline, the concurrent-multi-game-
sequence offline A/B (SS2.4) has NOT run yet -- do not flip the default
on without it.

16 new regression tests (kill switch, thread safety, sample-size gate,
bonus bounding, outcome proxy, ledger wiring with/without the flag).
Full existing test suite green (72 passed), orphan-solver lint passes
(49 live-reachable modules), mypy clean.

